be","phone_contact":"+32 2 648 10 49","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 au Charbon, 53","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Multidisciplinaire, Cabaret Mademoiselle est \u00e0 la crois\u00e9e des chemins entre le burlesque, les ann\u00e9es \u201830, le cirque et le freak show, les drag-queens et le stand-up. Un m\u00e9lange des genres \u00e0 la gloire du spectacle populaire dans une ambiance feutr\u00e9e et d\u00e9coiffante. La carte propose un assortiment majoritairement belge : des bi\u00e8res au f\u00fbt avec une mise en avant de micro-brasseries bruxelloises, des vins et une s\u00e9lection de spiritueux distill\u00e9s dans notre beau pays.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Cabaret Mademoiselle","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 au Charbon","address_street_number":"53","address_street_box":null,"email":"socialmedia@cabaretmademoiselle.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cabaretmademoiselle.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 648 10 49","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 au Charbon, 53","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Cabaret Mademoiselle","address_street_name":"Kolenmarkt","address_street_number":"53","address_street_box":null,"email":"socialmedia@cabaretmademoiselle.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cabaretmademoiselle.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 648 10 49","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Kolenmarkt, 53","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Multidisciplinair en ergens op het kruispunt tussen burlesk, jaren 30, circus- en freakshows, dragqueens en stand-upcomedy, kortom een mengsel van verschillende soorten populaire voorstellingen in een stijlvolle en toch ontspannen sfeer. Wat op de drankkaart staat, is voornamelijk Belgisch: bier van \u2018t vat en daarnaast bier van een aantal Brusselse microbrouwerijen, wijn en een selectie sterkedrank uit deze kontreien. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":30096,"location":{"lat":50.8462771,"lon":4.3485631},"last_updated_at":"2023-09-21T14:17:57+02:00","published_at":"2017-10-12T12:59:33+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/e1c35f23a4989163c106fa53bbffbc2f1678691b.jpeg","width":1131,"height":1600,"ratio":0.71,"oEmbed_height":1600,"oEmbed_width":1131,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"pt":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"en":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"it":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"cn":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"fr":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"sp":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null},"nl":{"title":"Red Alert","copyright":null}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2024-09-25","doors":"20:00:00","start":"21:00:00","end":"23:59:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false}],"prices":[{"translations":{"de":{"name":"Normal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"},"it":{"name":"Normale"},"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"sp":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"}},"value":30}],"date_exceptions":[],"closing_days":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[255],"translations":{"de":["Barrierefrei"],"pt":[null],"en":["Accessible"],"it":["Accessibile"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Accessible"],"sp":["Habilitado"],"nl":["Toegankelijk"]}},"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[]},{"id":5700000803,"date_start":"2024-09-25","date_end":"2024-09-27","date_next":"2024-09-25","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":true,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-09-09T12:53:16+02:00","published_at":"2024-09-06T08:42:29+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":306898,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"festival","ranking":1.100642416298209,"languages":{"spoken":["en","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":118,"translations":{"de":"Festival","pt":null,"en":"Festival","it":"Festival","cn":null,"fr":"Festival","sp":"Festival","nl":"Festival"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.batard.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000803"},"pt":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.batard.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000803"},"en":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","shortdescr":"In a world of crisis, injustice, and violence, we ask: how do we hold space for art, grief, rage, and hope? This edition of B\u00e2tard faces discomfort head-on. We invite artists who share our struggles, creating spaces to grieve, plot, and dream together. \n\nWe are not isolated islands; we slide together. \n\nJoin us SEPT 25-27 at Zinnema.","longdescr":"Sliding Islands\u00a0\n\nDear B\u00e2tard Community,\nIn this era of relentless crisis, injustice, and ethnic cleansing, we find ourselves wondering: are you holding up?\n\nSHORT REWIND\u00a0\n\nIn April, we postponed a season because of empty batteries and full cognitive dissonance.\u00a0\nBut so we\u2019re back, take a seat, a sip and lean into the collective discomfort.\u00a0\n\nLast year, we discussed the unleashing of emotional vampires. Today, we confront horrors in 4K, exposed for all to see. Our usual appetite for unexpected entrances, misleading paths, hacking discourse, and dismantling classism remains, but now we face pivotal moments.\u00a0\n\nWhat does it mean to host a festival amid ongoing genocides? What is the purpose of performing arts when international law and human rights seem more performative than ever?\n\nINTENTIONS\n\nThis year, we invited artists with the intention of supporting their growth and creativity, while co-creating spaces to grieve, plot and hope \u2013 artists who share our struggles, our questions, our anger.\u00a0\nThe same flesh, nerves, and bones navigate paradoxical territories on a daily basis, so let\u2019s bring them all into one space. We\u2019re not isolated islands, we slide together.\u00a0\n\nThis is an invitation to delve beneath the surface of what appears dystopian. Engage underneath what\u2019s visible at first glance\u2013 imagine islands, melting and merging, creating an archipelago of undomesticated bastards. Exploring new possibilities for defining, defending and sharing spaces \u2014whether physical, social, or mental.\u00a0\n\nARTISTS\n\nMilady Renoir, Araba bni Snassen, and Alexe Dols open their Maquis int\u00e9rieurs,\u2013 the inner struggles that define their activist and artistic practice, invoked by political and poetic friendships.\n\u00a0\nNabil Ennassouh draws a gesture of vulnerability that connects the biographical with the political, an attempt of love and abandonment.\u00a0\n\nVictor Dumont navigates affected matters, questioning our capacity to withstand a crumbling house while acknowledging our susceptibility to being overwhelmed. Eyes wide open.\n\nThe collective of C\u00e9line and Rose-Myrtha, Wildgroei Coven, will share their exploration of sisterhood, spirituality, witchcraft, and ancestry.\u00a0\n\nMarah Haj Hussein holds a workshop dealing with her research, struggles and questions around languages interlacing in one\u2019s mind in an oppressive environment.\u00a0\n\nFRIENDSHIP TALKS\u00a0\n\nLast but not least, we are introducing the new FRIENDSHIP TALKS : instead of the good old \u201cexpert aftertalk\u201d, each artist has chosen one close friend to engage in an open conversation about their artistic practices in ways that matter to them.\u00a0\nThe expertise will be rooted in affects. We are looking forwards to activate this new island with you all <3\n\nAs always, we are here with you, rooted in the present tense, ready to face the best and the worst together.\u00a0\n\nFrom Brussels, we send our solidarity from all rivers to all seas of liberation.\nBastardly yours,\n\nThe B\u00e2tard Team","performers":"Milady Renoir, Araba bni Snassen, Alexe Dols, Nabil Ennassouh, Victor Dumont, WildGroei Coven, Marah Haj Hussein, and more.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.batard.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000803"},"it":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.batard.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000803"},"cn":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.batard.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000803"},"fr":{"name":"B\u00e2tard Festival","sho